      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-27T22:20:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We actually have a feature on the AP that will alert the user when their cable is holding back their USB connection. I don\u0027t think it specifically supports DPAM 2.1 yet, but it could. \"Here\u0027s what I have but you can\u0027t do anything with it,\" is more or less what the the popup says.\n\nMore generally, I\u0027m inclined to maintain and transmit to the AP as accurate of a picture of the world as we can. If we\u0027re debugging something with DP later, especially if we don\u0027t have access to the peripherals in question, I\u0027d like to be able to easily distinguish between the scenario where the EC records the discovery incorrectly and where the EC chooses the wrong mode despite recording discovery correctly. The way this works now seems to blur that distinction.\n\nPrashant, what do you think from an AP perspective?",
      "parentUuid": "23a93411_a12d8868",
      "revId": "cbe321c1502d127cb9060bbdb9bb8979bef15d08",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
