      "writtenOn": "2023-07-19T23:32:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As a general comment for this file, I see a fair number of redundant checks, and I think the code would be easier to read if they were simplified. Here are some examples, although I\u0027ve probably missed some.\n1. Checking for the presence of the DP mode VDO in the same condition as checking `resolve_dpam_version`, which already checks the presence of the DP mode VDO.\n2. Reading `product_type` repeatedly instead of saving it in a variable.\n3. Repeatedly checking that the cable type is passive or active. IIUC, most of these checks only make sense if the cable type is passive or active. If the cable type is VPD or not a cable, the function should be able to return early.",
      "revId": "cbe321c1502d127cb9060bbdb9bb8979bef15d08",
