      "writtenOn": "2023-07-27T22:20:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d probably be OK with that change in interface for this function.\n\nLooking at it more closely, it might be more consistent with existing usage to call this function around https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/main/common/usbc/usb_pd_dpm.c#1252, where the DPM makes the choice of whether to enter DP mode at all. If you look above that line at the checks for USB4 and TBT, you can see that it calls `enter_usb_*` functions to check whether USB4 is supported and `board_is_tbt_usb4_port` to check whether TBT is supported. This function kind of reminds me of those functions.\n\nIn our existing code, when `*_setup_next_vdm` fails, it\u0027s usually due to some internal or protocol error that fundamentally prevents us from constructing the next message, not that we never should have tried this mode in the first place.\n\nIf there was something in the DP clause like\n```\n... \u0026\u0026 dp_partner_is_capable(port) \u0026\u0026 dp_cable_is_capable(port)\n```\nI think that would fit in OK.",
      "parentUuid": "086dc1ed_11893573",
      "revId": "cbe321c1502d127cb9060bbdb9bb8979bef15d08",
