      "writtenOn": "2023-07-27T22:20:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like, at least in the call site in `svdm_dp_config`, the code has already checked that the DPAM version is \u003e\u003d 2.1. I don\u0027t see a bit rate check, although it might be buried in one of the preceding function calls. At first glance, it seems like it would be possible to generate a Config VDO that has UHBR13.5 set, even though UHBR20 is not set, and that would be wrong.\n\nSince the DPAM version and bit rate are already at hand when the code calls this function, it seems easy enough to pass those in as parameters here. That would involve minimal additional code/work and make this function more obviously correct according to the spec.",
