      "writtenOn": "2023-07-27T22:20:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll comment on the function as it exists in Patchset 41. Obviously, if the logic changes, the comment might need to change.\n\nIt looks like the main points are\n1. If DP 2.1 is disabled or the cable is not emarked, entry is allowed (pre-2.1).\n2. If the cable is emarked and supports alt modes including DP or certain configs of TBT, entry is allowed.\n3. If the cable is emarked but doesn\u0027t support those alt modes, entry is not allowed.\n\n(The USB 2.0 part seems like an implementation detail to me. If a cable only supports USB 2.0, by definition, it wouldn\u0027t be able to support alt modes that require the SuperSpeed lanes.)",
